30,2,1,talk,Servas,,"My findings are sobering. We have a surplus of interest in modelling, but the trained phenotyping technicians have largely vanished into industry. Our senior analysts are also currently abroad.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
31,2,1,talk,Midori,,"I found that while shipping costs are rising, the agency still subsidizes glasshouse space. Also, the closeout files suggest that catalogue-style projects have much longer lasting utility.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
32,2,1,talk,Kenji,,"Oh no! The spectroscopy suite was broken for eleven weeks! But the animal facility is doing great and has a new vet. The glasshouses are totally full, though!","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
33,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"Interestingly, the repository is now very fast. However, the portfolio review shows that projects relying on live breeding colonies are far more likely to suffer schedule overruns.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
34,2,1,talk,Toshio,,"The closeout files confirm Midori's point on catalogues. More concerningly, field sites are highly unstable, with many losing entire seasons to fire or flooding.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
35,2,2,talk,Servas,,"@Kenji, the fact that glasshouses are booked solid combined with the loss of phenotyping technicians suggests a significant bottleneck for any plant-based research.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,2,talk,Midori,,"@Servas, that is a worry. If the technicians are gone, who will actually do the work in those glasshouses, even if we can get a spot?","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Midori, that's a good point! And if the spectroscopy tools are breaking down, any project needing high-end imaging might get stuck too!","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Toshio, your findings on field sites align with my data on breeding colonies. Biology is volatile. Computation, by contrast, seems to be the only stable path to a deadline.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Benjamin, I agree. The data suggests that the more a project depends on the whims of nature or live animals, the higher the risk of failure.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,3,talk,Servas,,"We must seek a path that aligns with our current strengths. If the human capital has shifted toward modelling and code, we should favor projects that utilize those skills.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,3,talk,Midori,,"I agree. We should also consider the long-term value. If catalogue-style awards provide a decade of utility, they are a much safer investment for the agency.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,3,talk,Kenji,,But we can't just do computers! We need to make sure the project doesn't need the broken spectroscopy tools or the overcrowded glasshouses.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Kenji, precisely. We are looking for the intersection of low operational risk and high technical feasibility.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,3,talk,Toshio,,"The evidence is pointing away from field work and live colonies. We need a project that is either purely computational or uses stable, indoor environments.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,4,talk,Servas,,"It is wise to be cautious. Let us see the candidates and apply these filters: avoid overcrowded glasshouses, unstable field sites, and the need for rare phenotyping staff.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,4,talk,Midori,,I'm ready. I hope we find something that is both useful for a long time and realistic to complete.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,4,talk,Kenji,,Me too! Let's find a winner!,"{""words"":6,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,I shall await the candidates with a measured amount of skepticism.,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,4,talk,Toshio,,I am ready to evaluate.,"{""words"":5,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
